and accepted the deal.

977
00:50:36,042 --> 00:50:39,375
In my family, they say I've always
been crazy but responsible.  I

978
00:50:40,292 --> 00:50:42,500
don't know how to eat one thing with the other.  I have

979
00:50:43,667 --> 00:50:46,083
made
seemingly crazy decisions,

980
00:50:46,167 --> 00:50:48,167
but I have always followed them through to the end.

981
00:50:48,250 --> 00:50:50,875
My mother says
that this is a good thing I have,

982
00:50:51,500 --> 00:50:54,833
that when I set a goal,
I go towards it.

983
00:50:55,417 --> 00:50:57,125
Until I see that it doesn't.

984
00:50:57,208 --> 00:51:00,375
If I see that it's not working, I'll give up,
but I'll try until the end.

985
00:51:00,458 --> 00:51:03,958
So, I think that day
was the happiest day of my life.

986
00:51:05,292 --> 00:51:08,792
I panicked, terrified.

987
00:51:09,458 --> 00:51:11,792
Because I didn't know what could happen.

988
00:51:12,542 --> 00:51:15,458
But we never know
what can happen, right?

989
00:51:15,542 --> 00:51:18,208
They say: “Study this career, it
has many opportunities.”

990
00:51:18,292 --> 00:51:19,208
Or not.

991
00:51:20,458 --> 00:51:22,750
Or in the ones that have exits
later you don't find anything

992
00:51:22,833 --> 00:51:23,917
because everyone has said:

993
00:51:24,000 --> 00:51:26,000
"I'll do this one, which has many exits."  Right

994
00:51:26,833 --> 00:51:27,667
?  You

995
00:51:28,417 --> 00:51:30,250
never know what will happen.  There

996
00:51:31,375 --> 00:51:35,583
is a question I always ask myself:
“Why not?”.

997
00:51:37,083 --> 00:51:40,250
It is an important stimulant.
When you suddenly say:

998
00:51:40,333 --> 00:51:43,583
“Look, how lazy,
because I think this is crazy.”

999
00:51:43,667 --> 00:51:45,958
If you say to yourself: “Why not?

1000
00:51:48,250 --> 00:51:49,750
Maybe it will work out.”

1001
00:51:50,333 --> 00:51:53,083
Okay, there are things
that are riskier than others.

1002
00:51:53,167 --> 00:51:57,375
Yes, obviously,
being an actor is a complicated path.

1003
00:51:58,167 --> 00:52:01,500
Now more and more, moreover.  There
are shovels of them, a hundred thousand of them come out.

1004
00:52:02,167 --> 00:52:05,542
The demand for actors is much lower

1005
00:52:06,208 --> 00:52:08,500
than the supply of actors.

1006
00:52:09,250 --> 00:52:12,875
But it's a life decision.

1007
00:52:14,542 --> 00:52:19,000
I think being consistent
with what you want

1008
00:52:19,708 --> 00:52:21,417
is the most difficult thing in the world.

1009
00:52:22,083 --> 00:52:25,583
Not everyone decides to do
in life what they want,

1010
00:52:25,667 --> 00:52:27,500
but what they believe is convenient.

1011
00:52:28,333 --> 00:52:32,083
So, when you take the risk
of wanting something and making it happen,

1012
00:52:32,958 --> 00:52:34,042
that's... No matter

1013
00:52:34,125 --> 00:52:36,875
how much you fail, you tried.

1014
00:52:37,833 --> 00:52:41,625
I knew I might not succeed,
but I would try,

1015
00:52:42,208 --> 00:52:44,625
until the end of my days if necessary.

1016
00:52:45,583 --> 00:52:48,792
I think this is the big lesson.  It was
given to me by my teacher,

1017
00:52:48,875 --> 00:52:51,875
my professor at the
drama school, Pepe Estruch.

1018
00:52:53,083 --> 00:52:55,750
That day when I told him:
“I don't want to leave here,

1019
00:52:55,833 --> 00:52:58,500
I want to stay at school forever”,
he grabbed me... He

1020
