put it against his chest and said:

1022
00:53:03,917 --> 00:53:06,750
“No one will kick you out
of this profession if you hold on.

1023
00:53:08,083 --> 00:53:09,208
Hold on.

1024
00:53:09,958 --> 00:53:12,000
This is a long-distance race.”

1025
00:53:13,500 --> 00:53:16,125
And then I said:
“Come on, the marathon.”  There's nothing

1026
00:53:18,000 --> 00:53:19,250
more,

1027
00:53:19,333 --> 00:53:22,708
it's the only thing you can say
to a person who likes this.

1028
00:53:23,750 --> 00:53:27,458
To me, people who say
they like performing... I don't

1029
00:53:27,542 --> 00:53:28,750
trust them either.  It

1030
00:53:29,542 --> 00:53:32,917
's not something you have to like, it has to
kill you,

1031
00:53:34,042 --> 00:53:36,083
you have to die for it.

1032
00:53:36,167 --> 00:53:39,417
Because it bends you from the beginning,
that is, it knocks you down.

1033
00:53:39,500 --> 00:53:41,083
If you say, "I like it,"

1034
00:53:41,167 --> 00:53:45,000
the first time they tell you no,
that they'll tell you that all the time, you

1035
00:53:45,625 --> 00:53:46,958
stop.  It must

1036
00:53:47,042 --> 00:53:51,042
be a passion, it
must be an act of faith,

1037
00:53:51,875 --> 00:53:53,625
believing in what is not seen,

1038
00:53:54,750 --> 00:53:57,792
which does not provide evidence
of its existence, believing in that.

1039
00:53:57,875 --> 00:54:01,000
If you don't have this,
the profession will throw you out in two minutes.

1040
00:54:01,750 --> 00:54:04,958
Then, my teacher, I remember that,
when we arrived at school...

1041
00:54:05,042 --> 00:54:07,208
We had a teacher in first grade.

1042
00:54:07,292 --> 00:54:10,583
They took it away from us because it was very big
and this teacher came in.

1043
00:54:10,667 --> 00:54:12,250
I felt a huge rejection

1044
00:54:12,333 --> 00:54:15,458
