with the first one we had.

1045
00:54:15,542 --> 00:54:19,375
That gentleman who replaced her didn't like
me from the beginning.

1046
00:54:19,792 --> 00:54:22,125
Rebellious girl, completely silly.

1047
00:54:22,667 --> 00:54:26,167
Why not?
He's a new teacher, maybe...

1048
00:54:26,250 --> 00:54:29,000
When he arrived, there were
about 20 of us in the class.

1049
00:54:29,708 --> 00:54:31,625
He said... He looked at all of us,

1050
00:54:31,708 --> 00:54:35,792
as I tell you to look,
one by one, and said:

1051
00:54:35,875 --> 00:54:38,542
"But do you really

1052
00:54:38,625 --> 00:54:40,542
think that you are actors?

1053
00:54:40,625 --> 00:54:41,667
Really?

1054
00:54:42,500 --> 00:54:43,792
Think about it for a moment. Do you

1055
00:54:43,875 --> 00:54:48,042
really think that you are
and that you will become actors?

1056
00:54:49,333 --> 00:54:50,792
Go home, okay?

1057
00:54:50,875 --> 00:54:55,375
At most and with a lot of luck, one of the 20.

1058
00:54:56,500 --> 00:55:01,083
Surely you are people in the profession,
amateur actors...

1059
00:55:01,167 --> 00:55:04,458
Actor or actress? One, with luck.

1060
00:55:05,875 --> 00:55:09,625
So, of your own free will,
start leaving."

1061
00:55:10,583 --> 00:55:13,333
And I said: "How cruel, the guy!

1062
00:55:14,500 --> 00:55:15,667
I really want it!".

1063
00:55:16,708 --> 00:55:20,417
He managed to get
35 of us to finish the class.

1064
00:55:21,333 --> 00:55:23,917
Not only did we not leave,
we stayed.

1065
00:55:24,542 --> 00:55:28,333
Now, I'm also telling you
that there are two of us left from that class.

1066
00:55:30,417 --> 00:55:32,083
Working today.

1067
00:55:32,167 --> 00:55:35,333
The rest dedicated themselves
to being theater people.

1068
00:55:35,417 --> 00:55:38,375
There are set designers, there are
people who write plays,

1069
00:55:38,458 --> 00:55:42,917
costumes, there's everything, producers...

1070
00:55:43,000 --> 00:55:45,208
But there are only two of us as actors.

1071
00:55:46,292 --> 00:55:48,792
The only thing I
can say to anyone who likes this

1072
00:55:48,875 --> 00:55:50,958
and wants to be an actor or actress

1073
00:55:51,042 --> 00:55:54,792
is to ask themselves
if they are really willing

1074
00:55:54,875 --> 00:55:58,833
to sacrifice
everything that needs to be sacrificed.

1075
00:55:59,542 --> 00:56:01,583
Many things are left behind.

1076
00:56:01,667 --> 00:56:06,583
And endure being told
no 25 times and

1077
00:56:07,250 --> 00:56:08,958
yes once.

1078
00:56:10,042 --> 00:56:12,292
Endure, ability to endure.

1079
00:56:13,375 --> 00:56:15,458
Training, without a doubt.

1080
00:56:15,542 --> 00:56:17,875
Study, work, preparation,

1081
00:56:17,958 --> 00:56:21,542
respect for your profession,
a lot of respect.

1082
00:56:21,625 --> 00:56:24,333
I see little respect
for this profession sometimes

1083
00:56:24,417 --> 00:56:25,875
and it makes me very sad.

1084
00:56:25,958 --> 00:56:29,417
In fact, even people,
the viewer, the receiver,

1085
00:56:29,500 --> 00:56:33,542
sometimes don't know how sacrificial
and hard this profession is.  It

1086
00:56:33,625 --> 00:56:36,792
seems like we're partying all day,
having a great time, like

1087
00:56:36,875 --> 00:56:38,875
this is happening as if nothing happened.

1088
00:56:38,958 --> 00:56:40,958
"A movie? There aren't that many."

1089
00:56:41,042 --> 00:56:43,417
No, sorry, I
get up at six in the morning,

1090
00:56:43,500 --> 00:56:45,417
I have to shoot at seven, I

1091
00:56:45,500 --> 00:56:48,583
put on my eyelashes
from seven in the morning, I

1092
00:56:48,667 --> 00:56:51,417
finish at 12 at night, I
get home dead.  You do

1093
00:56:52,042 --> 00:56:53,667
n't know what a shoot is,

1094
00:56:53,750 --> 00:56:56,583
only those
who have experienced it know.  You

1095
00:56:56,667 --> 00:56:59,333
don't know the effort it takes to
put on a theater performance.

1096
00:56:59,417 --> 00:57:02,042
It is a very, very sacrificial profession.

1097
00:57:02,125 --> 00:57:03,708
Sometimes you only see

1098
00:57:05,042 --> 00:57:06,750
the colors, the glamour.

1099
00:57:06,833 --> 00:57:10,042
"Look at that dress, it's at this party,
work with that one."

1100
00:57:10,792 --> 00:57:13,958
They have had to do many things
to be able to work in certain places.

1101
00:57:15,458 --> 00:57:20,208
Endure, love for this profession,
because it is an act of faith.

1102
00:57:23,083 --> 00:57:25,250
Hello, Blanca, my name is Araceli.

1103
00:57:25,333 --> 00:57:28,625
We really enjoyed
your characters and laughed.

1104
00:57:28,708 --> 00:57:31,333
But, in your life specifically,
what role does humor play?

1105
00:57:37,292 --> 00:57:38,458
It is fundamental.  I

1106
00:57:39,083 --> 00:57:41,083
laugh a lot in life.

1107
00:57:41,167 --> 00:57:42,833
Look, I also do characters...

1108
00:57:43,583 --> 00:57:45,458
Super serious and all that.  I laugh

1109
00:57:46,375 --> 00:57:47,708
a lot.

1110
00:57:49,417 --> 00:57:52,250
It's been like this since I was little,
my mother also tells me this,

1111
00:57:54,125 --> 00:57:56,667
